# 必考词 Unit07
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit07核心高频词汇

{{depart}}{/dɪˈpɑːrt/}}{v. 离开；出发}}{{The train departs from the station at 8 a.m.}}

{{department}}{/dɪˈpɑːrtmənt/}}{n. 部门；系}}{{She works in the marketing department of the company.}}

{{depend}}{/dɪˈpend/}}{v. 依赖；取决于}}{{The outcome depends on many different factors.}}

{{deposit}}{/dɪˈpɒzɪt/}}{n. 存款；押金；v. 存放}}{{You need to pay a deposit when renting an apartment.}}

{{depress}}{/dɪˈpres/}}{v. 使沮丧；使萧条}}{{The bad news depressed everyone in the room.}}

{{deprive}}{/dɪˈpraɪv/}}{v. 剥夺；使丧失}}{{The war deprived many children of their right to education.}}

{{derive}}{/dɪˈraɪv/}}{v. 源于；获得}}{{The word is derived from Latin origins.}}

{{describe}}{/dɪˈskraɪb/}}{v. 描述；描写}}{{The witness described the suspect to the police.}}

{{deserve}}{/dɪˈzɜːrv/}}{v. 值得；应得}}{{She deserves recognition for her outstanding contribution.}}

{{design}}{/dɪˈzaɪn/}}{v./n. 设计；计划}}{{The architect designed a modern and sustainable building.}}

{{desire}}{/dɪˈzaɪər/}}{n./v. 渴望；欲望}}{{He has a strong desire to succeed in his career.}}

{{desperate}}{/ˈdespərət/}}{adj. 绝望的；不顾一切的}}{{The desperate situation called for immediate action.}}

{{destination}}{/ˌdestɪˈneɪʃn/}}{n. 目的地}}{{Paris is one of the most popular tourist destinations in the world.}}

{{detect}}{/dɪˈtekt/}}{v. 发现；探测}}{{The sensor can detect even the slightest change in temperature.}}

{{determine}}{/dɪˈtɜːrmɪn/}}{v. 决定；确定}}{{Your attitude determines your success in life.}}

{{device}}{/dɪˈvaɪs/}}{n. 设备；装置}}{{The new device can monitor heart rate continuously.}}

{{devote}}{/dɪˈvəʊt/}}{v. 奉献；致力于}}{{He devoted his entire career to medical research.}}

{{diagnose}}{/ˈdaɪəɡnəʊz/}}{v. 诊断}}{{The doctor diagnosed the patient with a rare disease.}}

{{dialogue}}{/ˈdaɪəlɒɡ/}}{n. 对话；讨论}}{{The two countries opened a dialogue on trade issues.}}

{{dictate}}{/dɪkˈteɪt/}}{v. 口述；命令；支配}}{{Market forces dictate the prices of goods.}}

{{differ}}{/ˈdɪfər/}}{v. 不同；意见不合}}{{Opinions differ on the best approach to education reform.}}

{{digest}}{/daɪˈdʒest/}}{v. 消化；理解}}{{It takes time to digest the information from the lecture.}}

{{dilemma}}{/dɪˈlemə/}}{n. 困境；进退两难}}{{The company faced a dilemma between profit and ethics.}}

{{dimension}}{/daɪˈmenʃn/}}{n. 维度；方面}}{{The problem has both economic and social dimensions.}}

{{diminish}}{/dɪˈmɪnɪʃ/}}{v. 减少；缩小}}{{The influence of the traditional media has diminished.}}

{{diplomatic}}{/ˌdɪpləˈmætɪk/}}{adj. 外交的；老练的}}{{Diplomatic relations between the two countries have improved.}}

{{disapprove}}{/ˌdɪsəˈpruːv/}}{v. 不赞成；反对}}{{His parents disapproved of his decision to drop out of school.}}

{{discipline}}{/ˈdɪsəplɪn/}}{n. 纪律；学科}}{{Self-discipline is essential for achieving long-term goals.}}

{{disclose}}{/dɪsˈkləʊz/}}{v. 揭露；透露}}{{The company refused to disclose its financial records.}}

{{discount}}{/ˈdɪskaʊnt/}}{n. 折扣；v. 打折}}{{The store offered a 20% discount on all items.}}

{{discriminate}}{/dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt/}}{v. 区分；歧视}}{{It is illegal to discriminate against people based on their race.}}

{{disguise}}{/dɪsˈɡaɪz/}}{v. 伪装；n. 伪装物}}{{He disguised himself as a police officer to enter the building.}}

{{dismiss}}{/dɪsˈmɪs/}}{v. 解雇；驳回；不予理会}}{{The court dismissed the case due to lack of evidence.}}

{{disorder}}{/dɪsˈɔːrdər/}}{n. 混乱；疾病}}{{The patient was diagnosed with a sleep disorder.}}

{{display}}{/dɪˈspleɪ/}}{v./n. 展示；陈列}}{{The museum displays artifacts from ancient civilizations.}}

{{dispose}}{/dɪˈspəʊz/}}{v. 处理；布置}}{{Please dispose of the waste in the proper bins.}}

{{dispute}}{/dɪˈspjuːt/}}{n./v. 争论；争端}}{{The two countries are trying to resolve the border dispute.}}

{{dissolve}}{/dɪˈzɒlv/}}{v. 溶解；解散}}{{Sugar dissolves quickly in hot water.}}

{{distinct}}{/dɪˈstɪŋkt/}}{adj. 明显的；不同的}}{{The two cultures have distinct traditions and customs.}}

{{distinguish}}{/dɪˈstɪŋɡwɪʃ/}}{v. 区分；辨别}}{{It is hard to distinguish between the twins.}}
